@startuml Factory Method Pattern

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Factory Method Pattern - Basic Structure

' Abstract Creator
abstract class Creator <<Creator>> {
  {abstract} +factoryMethod(): Product
  +operation(): void
}

' Concrete Creators
class ConcreteCreatorA <<ConcreteCreator>> {
  +factoryMethod(): Product
}

class ConcreteCreatorB <<ConcreteCreator>> {
  +factoryMethod(): Product
}

' Product
interface Product <<Product>> {
  +operation(): void
}

' Concrete Products
class ConcreteProductA <<ConcreteProduct>> {
  +operation(): void
}

class ConcreteProductB <<ConcreteProduct>> {
  +operation(): void
}

' Relationships
Creator <|-- ConcreteCreatorA
Creator <|-- ConcreteCreatorB

Product <|.. ConcreteProductA
Product <|.. ConcreteProductB

Creator ..> Product : creates >
ConcreteCreatorA ..> ConcreteProductA : creates >
ConcreteCreatorB ..> ConcreteProductB : creates >

' Pattern component notes
note right of Creator
  <b>Creator (Abstract)</b>
  Declares the factory method that returns
  a Product object.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Declares abstract factoryMethod()
  • May contain template method operation()
    that calls factoryMethod()
  • Defines interface without specifying
    concrete product classes

  <b>Key Principle:</b>
  Defers instantiation to subclasses.
end note

note left of Product
  <b>Product (Interface)</b>
  Defines the interface of objects
  created by factory method.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Declares operations that all
    concrete products must implement
  • Allows Creator to work with any
    product variant
end note

note bottom of ConcreteCreatorA
  <b>Concrete Creator A</b>
  Implements factory method to create
  ConcreteProductA.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Overrides factoryMethod() to return
    new instance of ConcreteProductA
  • Decides which concrete class to
    instantiate
end note

note bottom of ConcreteCreatorB
  <b>Concrete Creator B</b>
  Implements factory method to create
  ConcreteProductB.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Overrides factoryMethod() to return
    new instance of ConcreteProductB
  • Provides different implementation
    than ConcreteCreatorA
end note

note bottom of ConcreteProductA
  <b>Concrete Product A</b>
  Implements Product interface.

  <b>Role:</b>
  • Provides specific implementation
    of Product operations
  • Created by ConcreteCreatorA
end note

' Pattern overview note
note as PatternOverview
  <b>Factory Method Pattern</b>

  <b>Intent:</b>
  Define an interface for creating an object,
  but let subclasses decide which class to
  instantiate. Factory Method lets a class
  defer instantiation to subclasses.

  <b>Key Concept:</b>
  The Creator defines WHAT to create (Product),
  but each ConcreteCreator decides which
  specific ConcreteProduct to instantiate.

  <b>How It Works:</b>
  1. Client calls Creator.operation()
  2. operation() calls factoryMethod()
  3. Subclass's factoryMethod() creates
     specific ConcreteProduct
  4. Client receives Product through
     abstract interface

  <b>Client Usage:</b>
  Creator creator = new ConcreteCreatorA();
  creator.operation();
  // Uses ConcreteProductA internally
end note

@enduml